#import "../template.typ": somatic_page

// PHASE 5 - PAGE 28: SELF-SABOTAGE - PROMPTS
// Mirroring technique + Mad-lib structured prompts per Shadow Work Philosopher

#somatic_page(
  title: "The Saboteur's Logic",
  body_text: [
    Think of the last time you sabotaged yourself. Notice where shame or frustration lives in your body right now—perhaps a sinking in the chest or a heaviness in the shoulders. This is the weight of self-betrayal. But beneath it lies a protector, doing its best to keep you safe.
    
    #v(0.5cm)
    
    #set text(style: "italic", size: 10.5pt)
    
    *1. A pattern of self-sabotage I keep repeating is* __________ *(procrastinating, overspending, pushing people away, quitting before I succeed, numbing out)*.
    
    I notice this pattern when I __________.
    #v(1em)
    #line(length: 100%, stroke: (dash: "dotted"))
    #v(1em)
    #line(length: 100%, stroke: (dash: "dotted"))
    #v(1em)
    #line(length: 100%, stroke: (dash: "dotted"))

    #v(0.8cm)
    *2. This pattern protects me from* __________ *(success, visibility, rejection, having to change, being truly seen)*.
    
    If I didn't sabotage myself, I might have to face __________.
    #v(1em)
    #line(length: 100%, stroke: (dash: "dotted"))
    #v(1em)
    #line(length: 100%, stroke: (dash: "dotted"))
    #v(1em)
    #line(length: 100%, stroke: (dash: "dotted"))

    #v(0.8cm)
    *3. If my saboteur had a voice, it would say:*
    
    "I do this because __________."
    
    "I am trying to keep you safe from __________."
    #v(1em)
    #line(length: 100%, stroke: (dash: "dotted"))
    #v(1em)
    #line(length: 100%, stroke: (dash: "dotted"))
    #v(1em)
    #line(length: 100%, stroke: (dash: "dotted"))
  ],
  image_path: none,
  layout_style: "bottom"
)
